# Pono @PACKAGE_VERSION@

A statically linked build of the [Pono](https://github.com/stanford-centaur/pono)
model checker for x86-64 Linux, which runs without any other files.

    $ ./pono --version
    @VERSION_LINE@

## Contents

- `pono`: the model checker.
- `smoketest.sh`: prints the version and the usage of `pono`, then runs it on
  the tasks in `examples/` and exits with status 0 if `pono` reports the
  verdict each task is named after.
- `examples/`: a MoXI task with a satisfiable query, `sat.moxi`, and one with
  an unsatisfiable query, `unsat.moxi`.
- `LICENSE` and `LICENSES/`: the licenses of Pono and of the software linked
  into it.

## Usage

    ./pono [<option> ...] <file>

where `<file>` is a model in Btor2, SMV, VMT, or MoXI format.
`./pono --help` lists the options. Pono prints `sat` if it finds a trace that
satisfies the query (violates the property), `unsat` if it proves that none
does, and `unknown` if it does neither.

